# The built plugin bundles are esbuild output, not authored source.
#
# Every one of them carries exactly four trailing-whitespace lines, and all
# four come from ONE place: a vendored dependency's own code-generation
# template (`zod`), where the whitespace sits inside a template literal and is
# part of the string that library emits. It cannot be stripped without editing
# what a dependency generates, and it cannot be fixed upstream from here.
#
# `git diff --check` is worth keeping honest for hand-written code, so the
# artifacts are exempted rather than the check being abandoned: whenever a
# source change shifts those four lines into a diff hunk, the check would
# otherwise fail for a reason no author can act on.
plugin/scripts/*.cjs -whitespace linguist-generated=true
